🚀 Terraform Secrets Management (Vault)

Overview

Terraform Secrets Management ensures sensitive data (like API keys, passwords, credentials) is NOT hardcoded in our infrastructure code.

Instead, secrets are securely stored and accessed using HashiCorp Vault.

🧠 Core Concept

Terraform needs secrets to provision infrastructure, but:

❌ Hardcoding → security risk
✔ Vault → secure, controlled access

👉 Secrets are fetched at runtime instead of being stored in code

🔥 Problem (Without Vault)

• Secrets stored in .tf files or state
• Exposed in Git/version control
• Difficult to rotate
• Security vulnerability

💡 Solution (Vault Integration)

• Store secrets securely in Vault
• Use policies to control access
• Authenticate via AppRole
• Terraform reads secrets using Vault provider

🏗️ Key Components

• Secret Engine → stores secrets
• Policy → defines permissions
• AppRole → authentication method
• Token → temporary access

